  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115668",
      "title": "Implementing Lifecycle Interfaces",
      "lectureOrder": 124,
      "videoOrder": 118,
      "sourceHash": "5760a8086cf4df031c86759d804f10088f359b05c1c065d91821591d400d61a3",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 2.64,
          "en": "Now, when using lifecycle hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.64,
          "end": 6.33,
          "en": "like ngOnInit, there is one potential problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.33,
          "end": 10.2,
          "en": "It's easy to introduce a typo like here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.2,
          "end": 13.35,
          "en": "the lowercase O, which is wrong,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.35,
          "end": 15.03,
          "en": "and you won't get any error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.03,
          "end": 18.36,
          "en": "because of course you can define methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.36,
          "end": 21.75,
          "en": "with any name of your choice in your classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.75,
          "end": 24.84,
          "en": "So defining this method here is not wrong,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.84,
          "end": 27.04,
          "en": "Angular just won't trigger it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.05,
          "end": 29.76,
          "en": "which is why if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.76,
          "end": 32.4,
          "en": "you might have an error in your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 34.743,
          "en": "that can be tricky to debug,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.58,
          "end": 38.4,
          "en": "because you're not getting any error message here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.4,
          "end": 42.15,
          "en": "and also not here where you ran npm start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.15,
          "end": 45.54,
          "en": "But still, the server status will now never change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.54,
          "end": 48.57,
          "en": "because the interval was never set up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.57,
          "end": 51.3,
          "en": "because this method was never triggered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.3,
          "end": 53.133,
          "en": "because you had the typo in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.36,
          "end": 58.53,
          "en": "To avoid hard-to-debug problems like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.53,
          "end": 63.53,
          "en": "it's recommended to use a specific TypeScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.81,
          "end": 65.73,
          "en": "that is embraced by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.73,
          "end": 68.97,
          "en": "when it comes to these lifecycle methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.97,
          "end": 73.97,
          "en": "You can add the implements keyword after your class name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.22,
          "end": 75.78,
          "en": "and that's now a keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.78,
          "end": 79.32,
          "en": "that does not exist in vanilla JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.32,
          "end": 81.9,
          "en": "It is a TypeScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.9,
          "end": 86.19,
          "en": "and it's used to implement an interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.19,
          "end": 89.28,
          "en": "which in the end means that you use an interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.28,
          "end": 90.96000000000001,
          "en": "which is another TypeScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.96000000000001,
          "end": 95.03999999999999,
          "en": "which we used before to define the shape of an object type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.03999999999999,
          "end": 99.15,
          "en": "and you can implement interfaces like that in your classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.15,
          "end": 102.993,
          "en": "to force your classes to have a certain shape.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.03999999999999,
          "end": 109.023,
          "en": "And Angular exposes an onInit interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.97999999999999,
          "end": 112.95,
          "en": "which you can import from @angular/core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.95,
          "end": 115.203,
          "en": "and which you must import from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.4,
          "end": 120.003,
          "en": "Now, OnInit is an interface, as you can tell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.26,
          "end": 124.47,
          "en": "and by implementing it into the class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.47,
          "end": 129.3,
          "en": "we force ourselves to implement it correctly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.3,
          "end": 132.9,
          "en": "which means we need to add all the methods, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.9,
          "end": 135.45,
          "en": "that are defined on that interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.45,
          "end": 140.45,
          "en": "so that are defined by the Angular team for that interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.7,
          "end": 142.68,
          "en": "And here, I'm now getting an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.68,
          "end": 146.31,
          "en": "because I'm not implementing this interface correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.31,
          "end": 147.9,
          "en": "If I take a look at that error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.9,
          "end": 150.63,
          "en": "I see that the property ngOnInit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.63,
          "end": 153.84300000000002,
          "en": "is missing in my ServerStatusComponent class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.98,
          "end": 157.773,
          "en": "and it's required by this OnInit interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.7,
          "end": 160.68,
          "en": "Now of course, I have ngonInit in it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.68,
          "end": 163.8,
          "en": "but I wrote it incorrectly, I got a typo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.8,
          "end": 165.45,
          "en": "As soon as I fix that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.45,
          "end": 168.99,
          "en": "and I have the capital O again, this goes away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.99,
          "end": 172.5,
          "en": "And that's why you should implement those interfaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.5,
          "end": 176.013,
          "en": "to protect yourself against unwanted typos like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 177.06,
          "end": 178.82999999999998,
          "en": "With that, again, if you saved it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.82999999999998,
          "end": 181.35,
          "en": "everything will work the way it did before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.35,
          "end": 184.68,
          "en": "and eventually the server status will change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.68,
          "end": 187.14,
          "en": "but now with help of ngOnInit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.14,
          "end": 189.483,
          "en": "implemented with help of this interface.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
